************************************************************
RELEASE NOTES FOR MICROSOFT LAN MANAGER VERSION 2.0 REMOTE
PROGRAM LOAD (RPL) TOOL KIT
************************************************************

When remote booting MS OS/2, one of the following
occurrences may be seen by a network trace using a sniffer:

     (a)  Open request for basedd01.sys is not sent by the
          workstation to the RPL server, thus disrupting the
          remote boot process.
     (b)  Open request for basedd01.sys is sent by the
          workstation, but the server does not respond.
     (c)  Open request for basedd01.sys is sent by
          workstation and received by server.  Basedd01.sys
          is opened, and a response is sent back to the
          workstation.  But the workstation does not
          acknowledge the receipt of the response in any
          manner.

Microsoft is still investigating this bug, and will send you
updates to the RPL software included in this kit, if the bug
is traced to this software.

In the meantime, it has been observed that if the network
adapter in the workstation is set to IRQ2, the remote boot
process proceeds normally.  It is recommended that you set
your network adapter to IRQ2 when you test your boot PROM
for MS OS/2 remote boot.  Remote booting MS-DOS should work
for all IRQ settings supported by your adapter.

Note:  The LAN Manager RPL server's network adapter need not
be set to IRQ2.  You only need to set the workstation's
network adapter to IRQ2.
